WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:08.560
From the start of 2017, the regulations around
small heated pools, such as spa pools and

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.080
hot tubs have changed and as long as they
meet the following criteria, they no longer

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.730
need to be fenced.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:20.100
Firstly to fit in this category – the need
to have an area of 5m2 or less and they need

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.030
to be designed for therapeutic or recreational
use.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:26.400
Then it needs to have a suitable cover.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.039
It must restrict the entry of children when
covered.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:34.050
Able to withstand a reasonably foreseeable
load.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.079
Able to be readily returned to the closed
position.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.960
And have signage indicating its
child safety features.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.360
Every wall of the pool must be higher than
760mm from the ground

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.840
and they must be difficult to climb.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:55.280
The tap or hose that is used to fill the pool,
must be fitted with a backflow preventer.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.350
These inexpensive devices stop water being sucked back into the mains water supply.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.690
Finally you'll need to register your pool
with the council for free.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:07.820
We’ll come and check that everything is
correct, give you one of these safety stickers

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.500
and then you're good to go.

